    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` a helper), and `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation on `POST /api/owners`, keyed on the `Idempotency-Key` header, using OfficeFloor function injection (no controller changes).\n\n**How it works** \u2014 when the header value has already produced an owner, the pipeline short-circuits and re-sends that original owner with `200` instead of running the create (which a repeat of the same identity would otherwise reject with `409`).\n\n**New files:**\n- `OwnerIdempotencyStore.java` \u2014 a thread-safe `@Component` mapping seen keys \u2192 created owner id. Process-wide, so it spans the separate requests of a retry.\n- `CheckOwnerIdempotency.java` \u2014 new entry step. Reads the optional header via `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")` (absent \u2192 `null`, no throw). On a hit it loads the owner and sends `ResponseEntity.ok(...)` (200); otherwise it takes a `@Flow(\"proceed\")` branch into the normal pipeline. This mirrors the framework's own validate-then-branch pattern (no `next:`, a single conditional output).\n- `RecordOwnerIdempotency.java` \u2014 runs after `SaveOwner` (id assigned) and records `key \u2192 owner.id`; a create without the header records nothing.\n\n**YAML** (`owners.POST.yml`): added the `idempotency` entry step with `outputs: { proceed: validate }`, and inserted `recordIdempotency` between `save` and `audit`. Both new steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]` to stay within the request's governance transaction like the surrounding read/write steps.\n\nKey design notes: the response step and the create-path responder never both run (hit XOR miss), so there's no double-send; keying purely on the header value matches the spec's \"a key already seen\"; and reading the header independently in both steps avoids threading a nullable variable through the pipeline.",
