    "probe_text": "Here is the full ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as the code stands. I've tagged each entry as **[validation]** (can reject the request) or **[side-effect]** (mutates the request, the owner, or external state). Steps from `dailyLimit` onward run under a `transaction` governance that commits once at the end; `CheckOwnerIdempotency` also runs in that transaction.\n\n**0. Security gate** \u2014 `authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` **[validation]**\nThe whole endpoint is guarded; a caller without the `OWNER_ADMIN` role is rejected before any function runs.\n\n**1. `CheckOwnerIdempotency`** **[validation/short-circuit]**\nReads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key already created an owner, it re-sends the original owner with **200 OK** and the pipeline stops (no duplicate created). Otherwise it takes the `proceed` branch.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerFields`** **[validation]**\nRejects with **400** (listing every offending field) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank, or if `address` is blank in *both* forms (`addressLine1` and flat `address`, checked against their normalized form). On success, publishes the body for later steps.\n\n**3. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** **[side-effect + validation]**\nConverts `telephone` to E.164 in place (strips separators, assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0` when no country code, requires 8\u201315 digits, and national-number length must match the country code). Rejects an unconvertible/wrong-length number with **400**.\n\n**4. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** **[side-effect + validation]**\nIf email present: requires syntactic validity, lower-cases it in place. Rejects an invalid present email with **400**. Absent/blank email is left untouched (optional).\n\n**5. `ValidateOwnerEmailDomain`** **[validation]**\nIf email present: rejects with **400** when its domain is on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\n**6. `NormalizeOwnerAddress`** **[side-effect]**\nNormalizes the address in place (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Prefers structured fields: non-blank `addressLine1` (plus optional `addressLine2`) composes `address`; otherwise the flat `address` is normalized.\n\n**7. `ValidateOwnerPostcode`** **[validation]**\nIf postcode present: must be exactly 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Otherwise **400**. Absent postcode accepted.\n\n**8. `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate`** **[validation]**\nIf `registrationDate` present and later than the server's current date \u2192 **400**. Absent is accepted (defaults at build time).\n\n**9. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** **[validation]**\nCounts existing owners whose registration date equals the business-day-rolled effective date; if \u2265 100 \u2192 **429**.\n\n**10. `DetermineOwnerHousehold`** **[side-effect]**\nComputes a deterministic `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` and publishes it. Inspects/mutates nothing else.\n\n**11. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** **[validation]**\nOver non-soft-deleted owners: rejects with **409** if an existing owner has the same identity key (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`), always; and rejects with **409** if an existing owner shares the same `householdId` (same last name + postcode) \u2014 *unless* the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, which bypasses this second block.\n\n**12. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** **[validation]**\nCounts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 **409**.\n\n**13. `BuildOwner`** **[side-effect]**\nMaps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; sets `registrationDate` to the effective date (supplied or today) rolled forward off a weekend to a business day.\n\n**14. `AssignOwnerHousehold`** **[side-effect]**\nStamps the computed `householdId` onto the owner.\n\n**15. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** **[side-effect]**\nSets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode, HASH8 from SHA-256 of E.164 telephone + last name), appending `-<n>` (n\u22652) to break collisions against existing codes.\n\n**16. `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`** **[side-effect]**\nSets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the fiscal year of the (rolled) registration date.\n\n**17. `CountOwnerNamesakes`** **[side-effect]**\nSets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**18. `FlagOwnerBulkSignup`** **[side-effect]**\nSets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than 80 existing owners already carry this owner's registration business day.\n\n**19. `FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate`** **[side-effect]**\nSets `possibleDuplicate=false` by default; skipped (stays false) for a declared household member or when no postcode. Otherwise, if an existing owner shares the same last name + postcode but a *different* telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest-created matching owner's id.\n\n**20. `SaveOwner`** **[side-effect]**\nPersists the owner via the repository (assigns its id).\n\n**21. `RecordOwnerIdempotency`** **[side-effect]**\nIf an `Idempotency-Key` header was sent, binds it to the new owner's id so a later repeat is served this owner. No header \u2192 records nothing.\n\n**22. `AuditOwnerCreated`** **[side-effect]**\nEmits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel and membershipNumber (membership fields read from the mapped `OwnerDto`).\n\n**23. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** **[side-effect / response]**\nSends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n---\n\nA few things worth flagging about the code as written:\n\n- **`DetermineOwnerHousehold`'s Javadoc says \"first 12 hex characters\" but the loop runs `i < 6`**, producing only **12 hex chars from 6 bytes** \u2014 so the doc and code agree numerically (6 bytes = 12 hex chars), just described confusingly.\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity` and namesake/duplicate counts include soft-deleted owners** (only `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` skips `isDeleted()`), so capacity/limit checks count soft-deleted rows.\n- **Idempotency short-circuit** re-sends with **200**, whereas a genuine create returns **201** \u2014 a repeat is distinguishable by status code."
